# The aLLManac — the LATEST channel.  Image pins, nothing else.
# =============================================================================
# The dev playground's pins.  See channels/stable.env for what a channel is.
# The rule for this file: a pin moves here FIRST, gets deployed to a box
# nobody teaches on, gets walked, and only then moves to stable.  What is
# here and not in stable is exactly the upgrade under test — keep the
# comment on each line saying what is being validated and since when.
#
# When this channel breaks, the deliverable is a minimal repro filed
# upstream (danny-avila/LibreChat) and linked from the pin's comment, not
# only our workaround — see the admin guide, "Channels."
#
# Still pinned, not `latest`: a moving tag would make "what broke?"
# unanswerable, and the answer is the whole point of the channel.
# =============================================================================

# Under test since 2026-09-15: 0.8.8-rc3.  What we are watching for — the
# Agent Management API with M2M auth (the seeder's forged JWT should go), the
# footer emitted with the HTML shell (the CUSTOM_FOOTER wall), OpenID
# discovery retries, the interface schema (the lockdown keys), memory as an
# agent capability, the design-system refactor vs. the branding asset mounts.
LIBRECHAT_IMAGE=ghcr.io/danny-avila/librechat:v0.8.8-rc3
# Everything below matches stable until there is a reason for it not to:
LITELLM_IMAGE=ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:main-stable@sha256:47afa74b495c802317712e5b8c8a65e7ca30c96636e9b618a5f8130eec72a8ee
RAG_API_IMAGE=ghcr.io/danny-avila/librechat-rag-api-dev:latest@sha256:c3e1a05bdd576b5000fa0e8a84a476e9858fa9219b2b5d78432ddce12c9fcf23
ADMIN_PANEL_IMAGE=registry.librechat.ai/clickhouse/librechat-admin-panel:latest@sha256:9a78851f84f448eab780ac658c4d17db51974c240492affc789a72d61e35f678
OPENCODE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/anomalyco/opencode:1.18.2

# ---- Datastores.  0.8.8-rc3 builds a partial index Mongo 7 rejects
# ("Expression not supported in partial index: $not") — upstream's own
# compose has shipped mongo:8.0.20 and meilisearch:v1.35.1 since 0.8.7, we
# were on 7 and 1.12.  Under test since 2026-09-15; stable's move is a
# data migration (Mongo FCV step, Meili dump) and gets its own plan.
MONGO_IMAGE=mongo:8.0.20@sha256:098862b1339f031900ca66cf8fef799e616d6324fa41b9a263f2ec899552c1ef
MEILI_IMAGE=getmeili/meilisearch:v1.35.1@sha256:8b57fc3c7f46535ddef3828df1538465ac19d892eb57c9a10da6df0880bd5856
POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:16-alpine@sha256:cf78e76683b9ca8c5733cbbdce6c9262b45b6767934dd0a95e671f9a0fc20685
PGVECTOR_IMAGE=pgvector/pgvector:pg16@sha256:ccc6e83d6e35e931dc7c5def2022729d5a6c370318d099181995567ff1fb4d6b
